        {
          "title": "What Is This Memory Useful For? Measuring Task-Conditioned Utility in Long-Term Agent Memory",
          "title_zh": "这段记忆有什么用？衡量长期智能体记忆的任务条件效用",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03930v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2611.03930",
          "summary": "The paper measures task-conditioned memory utility with a task-blind writer, a frozen reader that answers with and without a memory under identical filler, and a cost ledger for forming, storing and exposing memories. On LongMemEval-V2 web-agent memories, answer-bearing memories produce a mean paired reward gain of +0.33 over matched controls, but the gains do not extend to the tested software-engineering and scientific-coding benchmarks.",
