        {
          "title": "From Natural Language to Exact Cover: A Neuro-Symbolic Approach to Zebra Puzzles",
          "title_zh": "从自然语言到精确覆盖：Zebra 谜题的神经符号方法",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03641v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2611.03641",
          "summary": "The framework combines neural semantic parsing with deterministic exact-cover solving: an LLM translates a natural-language Zebra puzzle into structured tool calls that build an exact-cover instance, and a symbolic solver returns a solution or feedback used to refine invalid or under- and over-constrained encodings. The authors report that the hybrid approach consistently outperforms chain-of-thought prompting and recent neuro-symbolic baselines across model scales and families.",
