          "title": "Rethinking Next-Visit Diagnosis Prediction Beyond Aggregate Metrics: Retrieval--Memory Multi-Agent Adjudication",
          "title_zh": "超越聚合指标重新思考下次就诊诊断预测：检索—记忆多智能体裁决",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03826v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2611.03826",
          "summary": "LONGINUS combines evidence retrieved from patient records with structured memory of a patient's trajectory and uses cross-view agreement as a reliability heuristic to preserve shared predictions and adjudicate disagreements without revealing their source. Across MIMIC-III and MIMIC-IV with four LLM backbones, it reports the best transition-specific performance among LLM-based methods in nearly all settings while remaining competitive on aggregate metrics.",
